<docs-article
  title="Changelog"
  description="Notable changes to marko-ui components, the registry, and the marko-ui adapter."
  href="/docs/changelog"
  toc=TOC
>
  <h2 id="unreleased">Unreleased</h2>

  <p>
    <strong>marko-ui has not had a tagged release yet.</strong> The registry at
    <code>marko-ui.saulo.tech/r</code> tracks the main branch, and
    <code>marko-ui</code> is not yet on npm. Until <code>0.1.0</code> ships, treat component APIs
    as subject to change and pin your installed files by committing them — which, given that you own
    them, you get for free.
  </p>

  <p>Currently in the registry: ${COMPONENTS.length} components, plus the theme and utils items.</p>

  <p>Known gaps on the way to a first release:</p>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>chart</strong> — evaluated and specified (d3 primitives with Marko emitting SVG), not yet built.</li>
    <li><strong>navigation-menu</strong> — light-JS implementation; the animated viewport panels are not done.</li>
    <li><strong>scroll-area</strong> — styled native scrollbars rather than a synthetic draggable thumb.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="2026-08-11">August 2026</h2>

  <for|entry| of=ENTRIES by=(entry)=>entry.title>
    <div class="mt-8 border-l-2 border-border pl-5">
      <div class="text-xs font-medium tracking-wide text-muted-foreground uppercase">
        ${entry.date}
      </div>
      <h3 class="mt-1 text-base font-semibold tracking-tight">${entry.title}</h3>
      <p>${entry.summary}</p>
      <ul>
        <for|change| of=entry.changes>
          <li>${change}</li>
        </for>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </for>

  <h2 id="versioning">Versioning</h2>

  <p>
    Because component source lives in your repo rather than in a package you upgrade, marko-ui has
    two independent version surfaces:
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>The registry</strong> is unversioned and always reflects the current main branch.
      Components you already installed are unaffected by changes here — you take an update only by
      re-running <code>add --overwrite</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong><code>marko-ui</code></strong> is a normal npm package and follows semver. It is the
      adapter binding Zag machines into Marko, and it is the dependency that actually ships fixes
      to you.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    Before taking a component update, use <code>add --diff</code> to see exactly what would change.
    See <a href="/docs/cli">CLI</a>.
  </p>
</docs-article>
